    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0464" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v06/pg429"/>

                <head>133. Telegram From Secretary of State Vance to the Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d133-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-07-12T20:44:00+00:00">July 12, 1978, 2044Z</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p>Secto 8021. For the President from the Secretary. Subject: Private Meeting With
                        Gromyko.</p>
                <p>I am reporting by septel on arms control discussions with Gromyko Wednesday.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d133-f2"/> In a private meeting with him, I discussed the dissident
                    trials and delivered your oral message.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d133-f3"/> On the
                    slander charges against two U.S.
                        correspondents,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d133-f4"/>
                    Gromyko thought something would be
                    worked out. He was less sanguine on the Crawford affair.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d133-f5"/> He indi<pb facs="0465" n="430" xml:id="pg430"/>cated that
                    at some future time he would wish to discuss the handling of intelligence
                    matters, but did not think it useful to do so now.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Vance</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d133-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d133-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, Brzezinski Donated Material, Geographic File, Box 19,
                    U.S.S.R.—Prisoner Exchanges: (5/78–7/78). Secret; Cherokee; Immediate; Nodis. Printed from a copy that indicates the
                    original was received in the White House Situation Room.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f2" n="2" xml:id="d133-f2-content">
                <p>July 12; see <ref target="#d132">Document 132</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f3" n="3" xml:id="d133-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d131">Document 131</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f4" n="4" xml:id="d133-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d129-f2">footnote 2, Document 129</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f5" n="5" xml:id="d133-f5-content">
                <p>Reference is to F. Jay Crawford, a representative of International Harvester, who
                    was seized by Soviet police on June 12 on charges of currency violation. See
                    David K. Shipler, “Soviet Police Seize a U.S.
                    Businessman,” <hi rendition="#italic">The New York Times</hi>, June 14, 1978, p.
                    A6.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
